  "dom_id": "step-q109895",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & x=4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & x=5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}, & x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{5}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+{6}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =8+\\frac{25}{3}+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{67}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
